% Chapter 39 of the tariff: plastics and articles thereof — all twenty-six
% headings (3901 to 3926) and their 131 six-digit subheadings. A library: it
% includes gri.le, and tariff.le includes it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 18 (2026), Section VII note 2, Chapter 39 notes 1 to 11
% and subheading note 1, Chapter 59 note 2(a)(5), and the terms of the
% headings and subheadings (https://hts.usitc.gov/); the subheadings are the
% six-digit HS ones.
%
% The chapter has three parts, read three ways.
%   PRIMARY FORMS (3901-3914): a polymer in a form of note 6 (liquids,
%   pastes, dispersions, solutions; powders, granules, pellets, flakes, lumps).
%   The heading is that of the monomer that predominates (note 4) or of the
%   unmodified polymer (note 5); the subheading names the polymer — which
%   subheading note 1 settles (a named "poly..." needs 95 percent of its
%   monomer; a chemically modified polymer goes to "Other"). The facts:
%   "the kind of G is pellets", "the polymer of G is polypropylene" (a name
%   listed below), and where a subheading needs it the specific gravity,
%   whether expandable, plasticized, mixed with other substances, in aqueous
%   dispersion, chemically modified, its viscosity number.
%   WASTE AND SEMI-MANUFACTURES (3915-3921): the heading by the kind of
%   product (waste, monofilament, rod or profile, tube, pipe or hose, floor
%   covering, plate, sheet, film, foil, tape or strip) and what notes 8 to 10
%   require of it; the subheading by the polymer — "of polymers of ethylene",
%   "of polymers of vinyl chloride"... — and the features the subheadings
%   name (rigid, burst pressure, fittings; self-adhesive, in rolls, width;
%   cellular; reinforced or combined with other materials).
%   ARTICLES (3922-3926): sanitary ware and builders' ware by kind (notes 11);
%   3923, 3924 and 3926 by the article's PRINCIPAL USE (HTSUS Additional U.S.
%   Rule of Interpretation 1(a)), a judgment recorded with who made it and why
%   ("; judged", outcome last).
% The material of a composite good or a set is read from what it is
% classified as (GRI 3(b), gri.le). Chapter 39 note 2 sends many articles of
% plastics elsewhere — cases of 4202, parts of footwear of 6406, toys of 9503,
% textile articles of Section XI; those headings are outside the model, and a
% claim that the article belongs there is answered by the office (gri.le).
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a family* is a family of plastics goods.
    *a good* is a manufactured article; undefined.
    *a thing* is made of plastics; undefined.
    *a thing* is of plastics.
    *a good* is printed with motifs; undefined.
    the printing of *a good* is *a role*; judged.
    *a thing* is of cellular plastics reinforced by a textile fabric; undefined.
    *a good* is an article of plastics.
    the form family of *a good* is *a family*.
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*; judged.
    *a use* is a household use.
    *a good* is shaped as *a form*; undefined.
    the packing form of *a good* is *a form*.
    the polymer of *a good* is *a polymer*; undefined.
    *a polymer* is a polymer of *a monomer*.
    *a monomer* is a monomer of heading *a number*.
    the predominant monomer of *a good* is *a monomer*.
    the share of monomer *a monomer* in *a good* is *a number*.
    the base monomer of *a good* is *a monomer*.
    the polymer class of *a good* is *a class*.
    *a good* is chemically modified; undefined.
    *a good* is of an expandable grade; undefined.
    *a good* has been plasticized; undefined.
    *a good* is mixed with other substances; undefined.
    *a good* is in aqueous dispersion; undefined.
    the specific gravity of *a good* is *a number*; undefined.
    the viscosity number of *a good* is *a number*; undefined.
    the variant of *a good* is *a variant*.
    *a good* is worked beyond its surface; undefined.
    *a good* has a cross-sectional dimension exceeding one millimetre; undefined.
    *a good* is of rigid construction; undefined.
    the minimum burst pressure of *a good* is *a number* megapascals; undefined.
    *a good* has fittings; undefined.
    *a good* is combined with materials other than plastics; undefined.
    *a good* has a cellular structure; undefined.
    *a good* is self-adhesive; undefined.
    *a good* is put up in rolls; undefined.
    the width of *a good* is *a number* centimetres; undefined.
    the capacity of *a good* is *a number* litres; undefined.
    the subheading group of *a good* in chapter thirty-nine is *a group*.
    *a good* is an artificial gut.
    *a good* is a narrow roll.
    *a good* is a plasticized sheet.
    the subheading for polymer *a polymer* of variant *a variant* is *a code* under table primary.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a group* of *a class* is *a code* under table semimanufactures.
    the subheading for *a form* of *a class* is *a code* under table packing.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a use* is *a code* under table uses.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
