% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What a good is made of. Chapter 39 note 1: "plastics" are the materials of
% headings 3901 to 3914; Chapter 59 note 2(a)(5): plates or sheets of cellular
% plastics combined with textile fabric present merely for reinforcing are of
% Chapter 39.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule note_39_1 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a thing is of plastics
    if the thing is made of plastics.

% a good whose polymer the ruling names is of plastics
rule note_39_1_polymer with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "means those materials of headings 3901 to 3914":
a thing is of plastics
    if it is not the case that
        the thing is made of plastics
    and the polymer of the thing is a polymer
    and the polymer is a polymer of a monomer.

rule note_59_2a5 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 59,
        confer "Plates, sheets or strip of cellular plastics, combined with textile fabric, where the textile fabric is present merely for reinforcing purposes (chapter 39)":
a thing is of plastics
    if the thing is of cellular plastics reinforced by a textile fabric.

% an article is of plastics when what it is classified as consisting of (GRI
% 3(b)) is of plastics
rule plastics_article with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "shall be classified as if they consisted of the material or component which gives them their essential character":
a good is an article of plastics
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is of plastics.

% A polymer the ruling names without stating its form: the rulings describe
% resins and polymers in primary forms without saying so, and a good in any
% other form would be named by it (a film, a hose...). A presumption of this
% model, with no provenance: such a good is taken to be in a primary form.
rule plastics_form_presumed:
the form family of a good is primary form
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the polymer of the component is a polymer
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the component is a kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a manufactured article.

% the kind of product what the good is classified as consisting of (GRI 3(b))
% is
rule plastics_form with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "shall be classified as if they consisted of the material or component which gives them their essential character":
the form family of a good is a family
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the family of the component is the family.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The polymer. Note 4: a copolymer or a blend is of the heading of the monomer
% unit that predominates by weight; subheading note 1: within a heading, the
% same, among the subheadings of the series. A ruling that names the polymer
% says which; one that gives the composition lets the rules find it. (The
% monomers' shares are kept apart from the textile groups' of section_xi.le:
% a garment "contains 100 percent of polyester" too, and polyester is also
% the name of a polymer.)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the monomer family the polymer the ruling names belongs to
rule base_monomer_named with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "copolymers (including co-polycondensates, co-polyaddition products, block copolymers and graft copolymers) and polymer blends are to be classified in the heading covering polymers of that comonomer unit which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
the base monomer of a good is a monomer
    if the polymer of the good is a polymer
    and the polymer is a polymer of the monomer.

rule base_monomer_composition with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Polymers are to be classified in the subheading covering polymers of that monomer unit which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
the base monomer of a good is a monomer
    if it is not the case that
        the polymer of the good is a polymer
    and the predominant monomer of the good is the monomer.

rule note_39_sub_1_share with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "constituent monomer units of polymers falling in the same subheading shall be taken together":
the share of monomer a monomer in a good is a total
    if the monomer is a monomer of heading a number
    and the total is the sum of each percentage such that
        the good contains the percentage percent of a polymer
        and the polymer is a polymer of the monomer.

rule note_39_sub_1_predominance with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Polymers are to be classified in the subheading covering polymers of that monomer unit which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
the predominant monomer of a good is a monomer
    if the share of monomer the monomer in the good is a total
    and the total > 0
    and for all cases in which
            the share of monomer an other monomer in the good is an other total
            and it is not the case that
                the other monomer is equal to the monomer
        it is the case that
            the monomer at the total percent outweighs the other monomer at the other total percent.

rule note_39_sub_1_weight with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "which predominates by weight over every other single comonomer unit":
a monomer at a total percent outweighs an other monomer at an other total percent
    if the total > the other total
    and the monomer is a monomer of heading a number.

rule note_39_4_tie with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "If no single comonomer predominates, copolymers or polymer blends, as the case may be, are to be classified in the heading which occurs last in numerical order":
a monomer at a total percent outweighs an other monomer at an other total percent
    if the total = the other total
    and the monomer is a monomer of heading a number
    and the other monomer is a monomer of heading an other number
    and the number > the other number.

% subheading 3923.21: sacks and bags of polymers of ethylene
rule polymer_class_ethylene with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Of polymers of ethylene":
the polymer class of a good is ethylene
    if the base monomer of the good is ethylene.

% subheading 3923.29: sacks and bags of other plastics (or of plastics the
% ruling does not name)
rule polymer_class_other with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Of other plastics":
the polymer class of a good is other polymers
    if it is not the case that
        the base monomer of the good is ethylene.

