% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The variant of a polymer in primary form that its subheadings name. The
% rules are tried in order; the first that applies decides.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule variant_modified with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Chemically modified polymers are to be classified in the subheading named":
the variant of a good is modified
    if the good is chemically modified.

rule variant_dispersion with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "In aqueous dispersion":
the variant of a good is dispersion
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the good is in aqueous dispersion.

rule variant_expandable with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Expandable":
the variant of a good is expandable
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the good is of an expandable grade.

rule variant_plasticized with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Plasticized":
the variant of a good is plasticized
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the good has been plasticized.

% poly(vinyl chloride) mixed with other substances, not plasticized:
% subheading 3904.21 (nonplasticized)
rule variant_mixed with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "not mixed with any other substances":
the variant of a good is mixed
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and it is not the case that
        the good has been plasticized
    and the good is mixed with other substances.

rule variant_viscosity with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Having a viscosity number of 78 ml/g or higher":
the variant of a good is high viscosity
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the viscosity number of the good is a number
    and the number >= 78.

rule variant_low_density with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Polyethylene having a specific gravity of less than 0.94":
the variant of a good is low density
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the specific gravity of the good is a number
    and the number < 0.94.

rule variant_high_density with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Polyethylene having a specific gravity of 0.94 or more":
the variant of a good is high density
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and the specific gravity of the good is a number
    and the number >= 0.94.

% none of the above: the plain polymer
rule variant_plain with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Within any one heading of this chapter, polymers (including copolymers) are to be classified according to the following provisions":
the variant of a good is plain
    if it is not the case that
        the good is chemically modified
    and it is not the case that
        the good is in aqueous dispersion
    and it is not the case that
        the good is of an expandable grade
    and it is not the case that
        the good has been plasticized
    and it is not the case that
        the good is mixed with other substances
    and it is not the case that
        the viscosity number of the good is a number
        and the number >= 78
    and it is not the case that
        the specific gravity of the good is a number.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% headings 3901 to 3914: a polymer in primary form, in the heading of its
% monomer family (note 4) or of the unmodified polymer (note 5)
rule heading_primary_forms with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Chemically modified polymers, that is, those in which only appendages to the main polymer chain have been changed by chemical reaction, are to be classified in the heading appropriate to the unmodified polymer":
a good is described by heading a heading
    if the form family of the good is primary form
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the base monomer of the component is a monomer
    and the monomer is a monomer of heading the heading.

% note 7: waste transformed into primary forms is a primary form, not waste
rule heading_3915 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Waste, parings and scrap, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3915
    if the form family of the good is waste
    and the good is an article of plastics.

rule heading_3916 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "rods, sticks and profile shapes, whether or not surface-worked but not otherwise worked, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3916
    if the form family of the good is profile shape
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good is worked beyond its surface.

% a monofilament is of heading 3916 only when a cross-sectional dimension
% exceeds 1 mm (a finer one is a textile of Chapter 54); the heading's words,
% "any cross-sectional dimension exceeds 1 mm", lose a space in the PDF text
rule heading_3916_monofilament with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "of which any cross-sectional":
a good is excluded from heading 3916
    if the kind of the good is monofilament
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a cross-sectional dimension exceeding one millimetre.

rule heading_3917 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Tubes, pipes and hoses and fittings therefor (for example, joints, elbows, flanges), of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3917
    if the form family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [tube, tube fitting]
    and the good is an article of plastics.

rule heading_3918 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Floor coverings of plastics, whether or not self-adhesive, in rolls or in the form of tiles; wall or ceiling coverings of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3918
    if the form family of the good is floor covering
    and the good is an article of plastics.

rule heading_3919 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Self-adhesive plates, sheets, film, foil, tape, strip and other flat shapes, of plastics, whether or not in rolls":
a good is described by heading 3919
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and the good is self-adhesive.

rule heading_3920 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other plates, sheets, film, foil and strip, of plastics, noncellular and not reinforced, laminated, supported or similarly combined with other materials":
a good is described by heading 3920
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a cellular structure
    and it is not the case that
        the good is combined with materials other than plastics.

rule heading_3921_cellular with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other plates, sheets, film, foil and strip, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3921
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and the good has a cellular structure.

rule heading_3921_combined with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other plates, sheets, film, foil and strip, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3921
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a cellular structure
    and the good is combined with materials other than plastics.

rule heading_3922 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "similar sanitary ware, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3922
    if the form family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [bath, lavatory seat, sanitary ware]
    and the good is an article of plastics.

% a classification controlled by use is decided by the principal use (HTSUS
% Additional U.S. Rule of Interpretation 1(a))
rule heading_3923 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles for the conveyance or packing of goods, of plastics":
a good is described by heading 3923
    if the good is a manufactured article
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and the principal use of the good is packing of goods.

% a classification controlled by use is decided by the principal use (HTSUS
% Additional U.S. Rule of Interpretation 1(a))
rule heading_3924 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic":
a good is described by heading 3924
    if the good is a manufactured article
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and a use is a household use
    and the principal use of the good is the use.

% note 11: builders' ware is only what the note lists; a container only above
% 300 litres
rule heading_3925 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Heading 3925 applies only to the following articles":
a good is described by heading 3925
    if the form family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [door, blind, builders ware]
    and the good is an article of plastics.

rule heading_3925_containers with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Reservoirs, tanks (including septic tanks), vats and similar containers, of a capacity exceeding 300 liters":
a good is described by heading 3925
    if the form family of the good is container
    and the good is an article of plastics
    and the capacity of the good is a number litres
    and the number > 300.

% Note 10: plates, sheets, film, foil and strip of 3920 and 3921 are uncut or
% cut into rectangles, but not further worked
rule note_39_10 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "uncut or cut into rectangles (including squares) but not further worked":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [3920, 3921]
    and the good is worked beyond its surface.

% "Other articles of plastics": any manufactured article of plastics (a
% primary form, waste or semi-manufacture is no article).
% heading 3926: other articles of plastics and articles of other materials of
% headings 3901 to 3914
rule heading_3926 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other articles of plastics and articles of other materials of":
a good is described by heading 3926
    if the good is a manufactured article
    and the good is an article of plastics.

% Section VII note 2: plastics printed with motifs, characters or pictorial
% representations which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the
% goods fall in Chapter 49. Whether the printing is merely subsidiary is the
% office's judgment.
rule note_vii_2 with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "printed with motifs, characters or pictorial representations, which are not merely subsidiary to the primary use of the goods, fall in chapter 49":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and it is not the case that
        the heading is in [3918, 3919]
    and the good is printed with motifs
    and the printing of the good is primary.

table use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
kitchen use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
household use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic".
toilet use is a household use,
    as stated in HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "or toilet articles, of plastics".

% GRI 3(a). 3926 is the residual heading of the chapter's articles: every
% earlier heading that describes an article of plastics is more specific.
rule gri_3a_3926 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 3926
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3925.

% Sanitary ware and builders' ware are named by their own headings: more
% specific than the articles of 3923 and 3924 described by their use.
rule gri_3a_named_articles with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading an other heading
    if the heading is in [3922, 3925]
    and the other heading is in [3923, 3924].

% "Other plates, sheets..." (3920, 3921) are the flat shapes that are not
% self-adhesive: the self-adhesive ones are more specifically described in
% 3919
rule gri_3a_3919 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading 3919 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading is in [3920, 3921].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule plastics_subheading_primary with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3914
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the polymer of the component is a polymer
    and the variant of the component is a variant
    and the subheading for polymer the polymer of variant the variant is the code under table primary.

rule plastics_subheading_semimanufactures with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading >= 3915
    and the heading <= 3925
    and it is not the case that
        the heading is in [3923, 3924]
    and the subheading group of the good in chapter thirty-nine is a group
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the base monomer of the component is a class
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the group of the class is the code under table semimanufactures.

% the same where the polymer does not matter and is not known
rule plastics_subheading_by_group with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [3922, 3925]
    and the subheading group of the good in chapter thirty-nine is a group
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the base monomer of the component is a class
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the group of unknown is the code under table semimanufactures.

rule plastics_subheading_3923 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading 3923 is a code
    if the packing form of the good is a form
    and the polymer class of the good is a class
    and the subheading for the form of the class is the code under table packing.

rule plastics_subheading_by_use with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [3924, 3926]
    and the principal use of the good is a use
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the use is the code under table uses.

% the subheadings of heading 3923 name forms of article: boxes, sacks and
% bags, carboys and bottles, spools, closures
rule packing_form with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Boxes, cases, crates and similar articles":
the packing form of a good is a form
    if the good is shaped as the form.

% an article of heading 3923 shaped as none of the forms its subheadings name
% falls in 3923.90, other
rule packing_form_other:
the packing form of a good is other
    if it is not the case that
        the good is shaped as a form.

% The group the subheadings of 3915 to 3922 and 3925 are chosen by. Each
% heading's rule decides it for its own goods.
rule group_by_family with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "SEMIMANUFACTURES; ARTICLES":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is a family
    if the form family of the good is the family
    and the family is in [waste, profile shape, floor covering, bath, lavatory seat, sanitary ware, container, door, blind, builders ware].

rule group_casing with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Artificial guts (sausage casings) of hardened protein or of cellulosic plastics materials":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is casing
    if the good is an artificial gut.

rule artificial_gut with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Artificial guts (sausage casings) of hardened protein or of cellulosic plastics materials":
a good is an artificial gut
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the kind of the component is sausage casing
    and the base monomer of the component is a monomer
    and the monomer is in [cellulose, cellulose acetate, regenerated cellulose, natural polymer].

% subheading 3917.40: fittings for tubes, pipes and hoses
rule group_fitting with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Fittings":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is fitting
    if the form family of the good is tube fitting.

rule group_rigid_tube with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Tubes, pipes and hoses, rigid":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is rigid tube
    if the form family of the good is tube
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an artificial gut
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is of rigid construction.

rule group_pressure_tube with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "having a minimum burst pressure of 27.6 MPa":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is pressure tube
    if the form family of the good is tube
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an artificial gut
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component is of rigid construction
    and the minimum burst pressure of the component is a number megapascals
    and the number >= 27.6.

rule group_plain_tube with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other, not reinforced or otherwise combined with other materials, without fittings":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is plain tube
    if the form family of the good is tube
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an artificial gut
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component is of rigid construction
    and it is not the case that
        the minimum burst pressure of the component is a number megapascals
        and the number >= 27.6
    and it is not the case that
        the component is combined with materials other than plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the component has fittings.

rule group_fitted_tube with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Other, not reinforced or otherwise combined with other materials, with fittings":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is fitted tube
    if the form family of the good is tube
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an artificial gut
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component is of rigid construction
    and it is not the case that
        the minimum burst pressure of the component is a number megapascals
        and the number >= 27.6
    and it is not the case that
        the component is combined with materials other than plastics
    and the component has fittings.

% a flexible tube, reinforced or combined with other materials: subheading
% 3917.39, "Other"
rule group_other_tube with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Other tubes, pipes and hoses":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is other tube
    if the form family of the good is tube
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an artificial gut
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component is of rigid construction
    and it is not the case that
        the minimum burst pressure of the component is a number megapascals
        and the number >= 27.6
    and the component is combined with materials other than plastics.

rule group_narrow_roll with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "In rolls of a width not exceeding 20 cm":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is narrow roll
    if the good is a narrow roll.

rule narrow_roll with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "In rolls of a width not exceeding 20 cm":
a good is a narrow roll
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good is self-adhesive
    and the good is put up in rolls
    and the width of the good is a number centimetres
    and the number <= 20.

rule group_flat with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "plates, sheets, film, foil and strip":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is sheet
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a narrow roll
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a cellular structure
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a plasticized sheet.

rule group_plasticized_sheet with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Containing by weight not less than 6 percent of plasticizers":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is plasticized sheet
    if the good is a plasticized sheet.

rule plasticized_sheet with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Containing by weight not less than 6 percent of plasticizers":
a good is a plasticized sheet
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good contains a number percent of plasticizers
    and the number >= 6.

% subheadings 3921.11 to 3921.19: cellular plates, sheets, film, foil and strip
rule group_cellular_sheet with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39, confer "Cellular":
the subheading group of a good in chapter thirty-nine is cellular sheet
    if the form family of the good is flat shape
    and the good has a cellular structure.
